          {
            "id": 538,
            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-YybJd8AmQoTbIOxxs8nlqqfSgnh\">Looking at the two dominant age groups, in 1998, 16-to-30-year-olds accounted for 53% of the Internet users in Taiwan, compared to approximately 41% of those aged 31-50. Thereafter, the younger group's figures declined slightly over the next two years, reaching about 44% by 2000. Similarly, the proportion of Internet users aged 31-50 also decreased gradually, falling to roughly 37% at the end of the period.</div>\n</div>",
